.TH COSMIC-WICARA 1 "November 2026" "cosmic-wicara 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cosmic-wicara \- Native COSMIC dialog tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cosmic-wicara
.RI [ --help ]
.br
.B cosmic-wicara
.RI [ --help-general ]
.br
.B cosmic-wicara
.RI [ --dialog-type ]
.RI [ --dialog-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cosmic-wicara
is a native COSMIC dialog tool for shell scripts
version 4.2.2, reimplemented in Rust with libcosmic. It displays GTK-lookalike
dialog boxes on the COSMIC desktop and returns results on
.BR stdout (4).
It is COSMIC-only and Wayland-first; it does not run as a GTK application.
.PP
.B cosmic-wicara
shows at most one dialog at a time. All long flags mirror
.B cosmic-wicara --help*
(EN). Diagnostics are written to stderr; stdout carries data only.
Exit status is 0 on OK, 1 on Cancel/close, and 255 on error
(unrecognized option or missing/invalid dialog selection).
